<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Installs vs. Ratings - Interactive Scatter</title>
<style>
 body{margin:0;font-family:Segoe UI,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;background:#F4F7FB;color:#1b2a41}
 .wrap{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 18px 30px}
 h1{font-size:22px;margin:0 0 4px;color:#16284A} .sub{color:#5A6472;font-size:13.5px;margin-bottom:14px}
 .kpis{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:14px} .k{flex:1;min-width:150px;background:#fff;border-top:3px solid #2B6CB0;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 12px;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.07)}
 .k b{display:block;font-size:20px;color:#16284A} .k span{font-size:11.5px;color:#5A6472}
 .card{background:#fff;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.08)}
 .note{font-size:12.2px;line-height:1.5;color:#44505f;margin-top:12px;background:#FFF6E0;border-left:3px solid #E0A800;padding:9px 12px;border-radius:4px}
 .tip{font-size:12px;color:#5A6472;margin:8px 2px 0} #err{display:none;color:#b00020;padding:20px}
</style></head><body><div class="wrap">
<h1>Installs vs. Ratings (log-log)</h1>
<div class="sub">Google Play Store App Ecosystem Analytics - random sample of 5,000 apps (random_state=42, rows with a valid release date)</div>
<div class="kpis">
 <div class="k"><b>5,000</b><span>Apps plotted</span></div>
 <div class="k"><b>0.949</b><span>Spearman rank correlation (all points)</span></div>
 <div class="k"><b>0.941</b><span>Pearson r on log10 values (all points)</span></div>
 <div class="k"><b>~62.0%</b><span>Points at a repeated tier-median value (likely imputed)</span></div>
</div>
<div class="card"><div id="chart"></div><div id="err">Plotly could not be loaded. Open this file with an internet connection (it loads plotly.js from a CDN).</div></div>
<div class="tip">Drag to zoom, double-click to reset, shift-drag to pan, click legend items to show/hide groups, hover any point for app details.</div>
<div class="note"><b>How to read this chart.</b> Install values are tier lower bounds (1,000+, 10,000+ ...), so points form vertical columns; a small horizontal jitter (about +/-17%) is added for visibility and the hover text always shows the true tier. Grey points sit on the single most common ratings value of their tier, which is the signature of the notebook's median imputation of missing ratings; coloured points are the remaining (largely observed) records. The relationship is an association between adoption tier and feedback volume, not causation.</div>
</div>
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/plotly.js/2.35.2/plotly.min.js"></script>
<script>
